  --no-use                            do not make the new session active
  -h, --help                          display help for command

===== breakpoints help compact =====
Usage: dap-cli breakpoints [options] [command]

Manage source breakpoints

Options:
  -h, --help       display help for command

Commands:
  set [options]    Set breakpoints at source file line numbers
  list [options]   List breakpoints currently tracked for a session (per source,
                   with verified state)
  clear [options]  Clear breakpoints in a source (DAP setBreakpoints empty-list
                   semantics)
  help [command]   display help for command

===== stack help compact =====
Usage: dap-cli stack [options]

Get stack frames for a thread (auto-resolves to the stopped thread if
--thread-id omitted)

Options:
  --thread-id <number>    thread id (defaults to the unique stopped thread when
                          omitted)
  --start-frame <number>  start frame
  --levels <number>       frame count
  --name <name>           session name or id
  -h, --help              display help for command


Polling workflow:
  $ dap-cli status
  $ dap-cli events --after-cursor 0
  $ dap-cli threads
  $ dap-cli stack --thread-id 1
  $ dap-cli scopes --frame-id 1000
  $ dap-cli variables --variables-reference 2000


